@startuml TALOS_Release_Flow
title TALOS Release Flow (ADR-0029 / docs/deploy)
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #FEFEFE

|Developer|
start
:Push / open PR to main;
|GitHub Actions ci.yml|
:backend-lint (ruff);
:backend-test (postgres:17 + redis:7,\nalembic upgrade head, pytest --cov);
:frontend-lint-typecheck;
:frontend-test (vitest);
:docker-build + Trivy scan;
if (CI blocking jobs pass?) then (yes)
else (no)
  |Developer|
  :Fix and push;
  stop
endif

|GitHub Actions security.yml|
:CodeQL / gitleaks / pip-audit / npm audit\n(informational until baseline triaged);

|GitHub Actions deploy.yml|
:Build & push GHCR images\nghcr.io/.../trinetra-backend\nghcr.io/.../trinetra-web;
:Call Coolify deploy webhook\n(COOLIFY_DEPLOY_WEBHOOK_URL);

|Coolify on Hetzner|
:Pull git source at ref;
:Build from docker-compose.prod.yml;
:Replace running containers;\nvolumes persist;

|On-call / Admin|
:Verify /health /ready + login\n(VERIFICATION_CHECKLIST.md);

if (Healthy?) then (yes)
  :Release complete;
  stop
else (no)
  :Rollback Path A: redeploy last good ref\nvia workflow_dispatch or Coolify UI;
  if (Needs history fix?) then (yes)
    :Rollback Path B: git revert + push;
  endif
  note right
    DB migrations never auto-rollback.
    alembic downgrade is manual only.
  end note
  stop
endif

@enduml
